{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"blind_id\":\"HOX019\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Correctly contrasts ICAV sub-fund accounts and AGM dispensation with the plc’s umbrella accounts and AGM.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Correctly states that an ICAV can elect partnership treatment and an investment plc is per-se corporate for US tax.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":\"“This is often done per sub-fund, avoiding PFIC treatment for US investors” — overstates the investor tax outcome; an election does not automatically establish a particular investor’s tax treatment.\",\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"Both required points are covered, but the overclaim about avoiding PFIC treatment is a material local falsehood and caps the grade at partial.\"}"}}
